3446
01:59:46.393 --> 01:59:47.460
High.

3447
01:59:47.460 --> 01:59:48.293
I think it's high.

3448
01:59:48.293 --> 01:59:49.126
Yeah.
Yeah.

3449
01:59:49.126 --> 01:59:50.090
I hope so.

3450
01:59:50.090 --> 01:59:51.710
I hope I-
Extend it, right?

3451
01:59:51.710 --> 01:59:52.543
Huh?

3452
01:59:52.543 --> 01:59:53.376
Extend it.

3453
01:59:53.376 --> 01:59:55.100
Does Ben seem young to you?
I'm jealous.

3454
01:59:55.100 --> 01:59:56.240
Or is Ben mid-career?

3455
01:59:56.240 --> 01:59:57.073
I don't know.

3456
01:59:57.073 --> 01:59:57.906
I can't tell.

3457
01:59:57.906 --> 01:59:58.739
I can't tell.

3458
01:59:58.739 --> 01:59:59.780
He didn't, he didn't leave his age, right?

3459
01:59:59.780 --> 02:00:01.124
No.

3460
02:00:01.124 --> 02:00:02.420
Well, he had a job,

3461
02:00:02.420 --> 02:00:04.590
so he's not like just graduating from college

3462
02:00:04.590 --> 02:00:05.423
or something like that.

3463
02:00:05.423 --> 02:00:06.943
I feel like it's the first job out of college though.

3464
02:00:06.943 --> 02:00:07.873
I think so.
First or second.

3465
02:00:07.873 --> 02:00:12.267
I pin him at maybe 24, 25.

3466
02:00:12.267 --> 02:00:14.065
Okay, mid- 20s, yeah.

3467
02:00:14.065 --> 02:00:15.730
I hope we're not way off on that.

3468
02:00:15.730 --> 02:00:16.775
No.

3469
02:00:16.775 --> 02:00:18.730
I suspect mid twenties,

3470
02:00:18.730 --> 02:00:19.980
but thanks for the question, Ben.

3471
02:00:19.980 --> 02:00:21.800
I am jealous.

3472
02:00:21.800 --> 02:00:24.940
That sounds like such a cool opportunity

3473
02:00:24.940 --> 02:00:28.490
to just hit the road four months.

3474
02:00:28.490 --> 02:00:29.938
The world is your oyster.

3475
02:00:29.938 --> 02:00:31.238
Like yes, me too.|
You know what I mean?

3476
02:00:31.238 --> 02:00:33.260
When life was simple, Adam.
Quit Job, pack car.

3477
02:00:33.260 --> 02:00:34.660
When life was simple.

3478
02:00:34.660 --> 02:00:36.390
Hey, we had our run.

3479
02:00:36.390 --> 02:00:37.620
I know we did, right?

3480
02:00:37.620 --> 02:00:38.453
Yes.

3481
02:00:38.453 --> 02:00:39.286
I'm happy where I'm at.

3482
02:00:39.286 --> 02:00:40.119
I'm good.

3483
02:00:40.119 --> 02:00:40.952
It's okay.

3484
02:00:40.952 --> 02:00:41.840
I'm sorry, Ben.

3485
02:00:41.840 --> 02:00:42.914
We're back to ourselves.

3486
02:00:42.914 --> 02:00:43.792
Yeah.

3487
02:00:43.792 --> 02:00:45.010
(men laughing)

3488
02:00:45.010 --> 02:00:47.160
Books, books.

3489
02:00:47.160 --> 02:00:50.721
You can't go on a four month road trip.

3490
02:00:50.721 --> 02:00:55.721
This lighting out on the frontier in a journey

3491
02:00:57.610 --> 02:00:58.810
of self-discovery.

3492
02:00:58.810 --> 02:00:59.660
Head west.

3493
02:00:59.660 --> 02:01:03.320
Without reading "On the Road" by Jack Kerouac.

3494
02:01:03.320 --> 02:01:05.920
Are you even allowed to go on a four month road trip

3495
02:01:05.920 --> 02:01:08.330
as a young man?
Without "On the Road?"

3496
02:01:08.330 --> 02:01:10.397
Without having read "On the Road?"

3497
02:01:10.397 --> 02:01:13.680
I mean "On the Road" is seminal book for me,

3498
02:01:13.680 --> 02:01:16.128
I've probably read it 10 times.

3499
02:01:16.128 --> 02:01:18.227
I didn't include that on my list since you had first,

3500
02:01:18.227 --> 02:01:20.718
you had first dibs.
It's such a Gen X,

3501
02:01:20.718 --> 02:01:23.380
It's a Gen X, Boomer referral though, is it not?

3502
02:01:23.380 --> 02:01:24.213
It is.

3503
02:01:24.213 --> 02:01:25.460
It might be, it may,

3504
02:01:25.460 --> 02:01:26.910
has that book been canceled?

3505
02:01:26.910 --> 02:01:28.526
Can we check the cancellation file?

3506
02:01:28.526 --> 02:01:29.806
(Rich laughing)

3507
02:01:29.806 --> 02:01:31.690
I think it's okay still.

3508
02:01:31.690 --> 02:01:33.791
Who's in charge of the cancellation vault?

3509
02:01:33.791 --> 02:01:34.624
I think that one's all right.

3510
02:01:34.624 --> 02:01:35.650
I think it is too.

3511
02:01:35.650 --> 02:01:36.890
Yeah.

3512
02:01:36.890 --> 02:01:38.166
So I would recommend that, but you,

3513
02:01:38.166 --> 02:01:39.560
sorry I was like,

3514
02:01:39.560 --> 02:01:41.160
you were about to say something else.

3515
02:01:41.160 --> 02:01:43.140
No, I think it's a great question.

3516
02:01:43.140 --> 02:01:45.160
I think it's a two parter, go for it.

3517
02:01:45.160 --> 02:01:47.120
You have a few books down here.

3518
02:01:47.120 --> 02:01:48.310
Right, well I'm just thinking,

3519
02:01:48.310 --> 02:01:49.143
okay Ben,

3520
02:01:49.143 --> 02:01:50.920
what's going on in Ben's life that he decided

3521
02:01:50.920 --> 02:01:51.753
to quit his job,

3522
02:01:51.753 --> 02:01:54.020
pack everything up and like head out on the road.

3523
02:01:54.020 --> 02:01:58.120
Well obviously, it feels like an inflection point

3524
02:01:58.120 --> 02:02:00.790
where he wants to go inward a little bit

3525
02:02:00.790 --> 02:02:02.940
and figure out what the next thing is.

3526
02:02:02.940 --> 02:02:05.530
Or maybe connect a little bit more deeply

3527
02:02:05.530 --> 02:02:06.387
with who he is.

3528
02:02:06.387 --> 02:02:09.910
And so one of the books that you would recommend somebody

3529
02:02:09.910 --> 02:02:12.327
who's playing around with that,

3530
02:02:12.327 --> 02:02:13.257
"On the Road,"

3531
02:02:13.257 --> 02:02:14.800
because you're on the road.

3532
02:02:14.800 --> 02:02:16.040
Right?

3533
02:02:16.040 --> 02:02:18.842
Why not "A Man's Search for Meaning" by Viktor Frankl.

3534
02:02:18.842 --> 02:02:22.750
Tops everybody's list who's grappling

3535
02:02:22.750 --> 02:02:24.090
with these ideas, I think.

3536
02:02:24.090 --> 02:02:25.587
And one of my favorites also,

3537
02:02:25.587 --> 02:02:29.007
"Autobiography of a Yogi" by Paramahansa Yogananda.

3538
02:02:29.007 --> 02:02:30.517
I wanted to like that one.

3539
02:02:30.517 --> 02:02:32.481
And I couldn't get through it.
Couldn't get behind it?

3540
02:02:32.481 --> 02:02:33.473
Too magical.

3541
02:02:33.473 --> 02:02:34.875
Too crazy.

3542
02:02:34.875 --> 02:02:36.810
I think my problem with it

3543
02:02:36.810 --> 02:02:40.287
is every chapter ended well.
It's very dense.

3544
02:02:40.287 --> 02:02:42.110
Because his life was,

3545
02:02:42.110 --> 02:02:44.060
he was a magnificent human being.

3546
02:02:44.060 --> 02:02:46.210
I'm very, a big fan of Paramahansa Yogananda.

3547
02:02:46.210 --> 02:02:48.000
I just didn't get through the entire autobiography.

3548
02:02:48.000 --> 02:02:52.330
I think it's just a cool book to expand

3549
02:02:52.330 --> 02:02:56.220
your sense of possibility

3550
02:02:56.220 --> 02:02:59.660
and develop some appreciation for the mystical.

3551
02:02:59.660 --> 02:03:02.500
So my, you wanna hear a Paramahansa Yogananda story?

3552
02:03:02.500 --> 02:03:03.333
I do.

3553
02:03:03.333 --> 02:03:05.033
Before we get into finish this question.

3554
02:03:06.160 --> 02:03:09.620
So during, I think it was during the LA Yoga days,

3555
02:03:09.620 --> 02:03:11.342
when we first started LA Yoga magazine,

3556
02:03:11.342 --> 02:03:13.990
I set up a meeting with the head

3557
02:03:13.990 --> 02:03:16.240
of the Self-Realization Fellowship at the time.

3558
02:03:16.240 --> 02:03:18.341
I think it was number, maybe it was number two.

3559
02:03:18.341 --> 02:03:21.100
And their headquarters are in Mount Washington

3560
02:03:21.100 --> 02:03:21.933
in Los Angeles,

3561
02:03:21.933 --> 02:03:23.370
which was the original house,

3562
02:03:23.370 --> 02:03:25.460
the original estate before any of the others.

3563
02:03:25.460 --> 02:03:28.666
That's where he set, Paramahansa Yogananda, set up shop.

3564
02:03:28.666 --> 02:03:32.710
And we were supposed to have our meeting in the boardroom

3565
02:03:32.710 --> 02:03:35.810
which has like all these really cool artifacts and stuff.

3566
02:03:35.810 --> 02:03:37.210
And I was really excited to sit there

3567
02:03:37.210 --> 02:03:38.370
and have this conversation,

3568
02:03:38.370 --> 02:03:39.639
but we got booted.

3569
02:03:39.639 --> 02:03:41.940
And I was a little disappointed, but he goes,

3570
02:03:41.940 --> 02:03:43.020
let's sit by the fireplace.

3571
02:03:43.020 --> 02:03:45.450
And the guy wasn't particularly warm or anything,

3572
02:03:45.450 --> 02:03:47.260
or like memorable,

3573
02:03:47.260 --> 02:03:49.744
but he said a lot of people say after,

3574
02:03:49.744 --> 02:03:52.314
he used to spend every evening down here having tea

3575
02:03:52.314 --> 02:03:55.290
by the fireplace every evening

3576
02:03:55.290 --> 02:03:56.750
and had whoever guests came through,

3577
02:03:56.750 --> 02:03:58.020
that's where he'd spend his time.

3578
02:03:58.020 --> 02:03:59.248
And they say you,

3579
02:03:59.248 --> 02:04:01.833
people can feel his presence sometimes.

3580
02:04:01.833 --> 02:04:03.393
And at the time,

3581
02:04:03.393 --> 02:04:07.090
I wasn't particularly a huge Paramahansa Yogananda guy

3582
02:04:07.090 --> 02:04:09.762
'cause he was merging his worldview with Jesus,

3583
02:04:09.762 --> 02:04:14.160
and trying to make yoga more palatable by using Christianity

3584
02:04:14.160 --> 02:04:16.170
as some sort of a Trojan horse say,

3585
02:04:16.170 --> 02:04:17.030
or not even a Trojan,

3586
02:04:17.030 --> 02:04:18.270
that's a disrespectful way of putting it.

3587
02:04:18.270 --> 02:04:21.474
But to show the, how they fit together.

3588
02:04:21.474 --> 02:04:26.474
And so I was like pretty new to that world,

3589
02:04:27.620 --> 02:04:28.790
had my interview with him.

3590
02:04:28.790 --> 02:04:31.160
Like I said, he was not super impressed with me.

3591
02:04:31.160 --> 02:04:32.497
I didn't really like him that much.

3592
02:04:32.497 --> 02:04:33.500
(Rich laughing)

3593
02:04:33.500 --> 02:04:35.017
But then we finished the interview fine.

3594
02:04:35.017 --> 02:04:39.580
And I get up, and walking out the door,

3595
02:04:39.580 --> 02:04:42.490
and I'm like physically high,

3596
02:04:42.490 --> 02:04:45.710
like I'm floating out of my body kind of high.

3597
02:04:45.710 --> 02:04:47.773
Like I'm just like, light headed.

3598
02:04:47.773 --> 02:04:48.655
Wow.

3599
02:04:48.655 --> 02:04:49.488
Like my, all my energy,

3600
02:04:49.488 --> 02:04:50.520
exact flow state kind of stuff.

3601
02:04:50.520 --> 02:04:52.990
Like seriously, like time slowed down.

3602
02:04:52.990 --> 02:04:54.660
I felt it a few times in my life,

3603
02:04:54.660 --> 02:04:56.110
but this was very profound.

3604
02:04:56.110 --> 02:04:56.943
Wow.

3605
02:04:56.943 --> 02:04:58.930
And not, no drugs, no nothing.

3606
02:04:58.930 --> 02:05:01.828
Like it felt like the coming on of a psychedelic trip

3607
02:05:01.828 --> 02:05:03.540
without taking any drugs.

3608
02:05:03.540 --> 02:05:04.373
That's what it felt like.

3609
02:05:04.373 --> 02:05:05.641
So what do you make of that?

3610
02:05:05.641 --> 02:05:07.210
Yogananda.

3611
02:05:07.210 --> 02:05:08.440
Yeah.
Yeah, no question.

3612
02:05:08.440 --> 02:05:09.273
That's a trip, man.

3613
02:05:09.273 --> 02:05:10.106
Isn't that cool?

3614
02:05:10.106 --> 02:05:10.939
That is a trip.

3615
02:05:10.939 --> 02:05:13.705
So for people that don't know Paramahansa Yogananda

3616
02:05:13.705 --> 02:05:14.960
was many things,

3617
02:05:14.960 --> 02:05:19.960
but he was one of the initial people to come from India

3618
02:05:21.630 --> 02:05:23.830
to the United States and was part of the movement

3619
02:05:23.830 --> 02:05:25.592
of introducing yoga and meditation

3620
02:05:25.592 --> 02:05:28.410
and all these things that have become so integrated

3621
02:05:28.410 --> 02:05:30.150
into our culture at a time when these

3622
02:05:30.150 --> 02:05:31.910
were crazy brand new ideas.

3623
02:05:31.910 --> 02:05:33.720
Yeah, and that, like the 1920s,

3624
02:05:33.720 --> 02:05:34.957
he was coming here and-

3625
02:05:34.957 --> 02:05:37.630
And he would sit in these salons in Manhattan

3626
02:05:37.630 --> 02:05:40.865
and have these get togethers that are reminiscent of

3627
02:05:40.865 --> 02:05:42.935
that movie, "The Master."

3628
02:05:42.935 --> 02:05:43.768
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

3629
02:05:43.768 --> 02:05:45.010
That's what comes to mind,

3630
02:05:45.010 --> 02:05:46.748
like what that vibe must have been like.

3631
02:05:46.748 --> 02:05:50.966
But just a beautiful, magnificent consciousness.

3632
02:05:50.966 --> 02:05:53.610
There's that headquarters on Mount Washington,

3633
02:05:53.610 --> 02:05:56.920
but there's also the Self-Realization Retreat Center

3634
02:05:56.920 --> 02:05:59.690
in Pacific Palisades where you can,

3635
02:05:59.690 --> 02:06:00.730
the grounds are open,

3636
02:06:00.730 --> 02:06:02.775
and there's this pond and you can go and meditate there.

3637
02:06:02.775 --> 02:06:05.580
And also the temple in Encinitas,

3638
02:06:05.580 --> 02:06:06.470
it's right on the beach.
Which is my favorite one.

3639
02:06:06.470 --> 02:06:10.024
Which is the surf spot right off of it.

3640
02:06:10.024 --> 02:06:10.857
Swami's.
It's called Swami's.

3641
02:06:10.857 --> 02:06:12.610
And I think a lot of people don't know that that's why

3642
02:06:12.610 --> 02:06:13.443
it's called Swami's.

3643
02:06:13.443 --> 02:06:14.276
No, I agree, but that-

3644
02:06:14.276 --> 02:06:15.820
'Cause he is the Swami.

3645
02:06:15.820 --> 02:06:18.270
So if you don't read the book, Ben,

3646
02:06:18.270 --> 02:06:20.859
make sure you stop by one of his sites.

3647
02:06:20.859 --> 02:06:21.727
You should go.

3648
02:06:21.727 --> 02:06:22.560
Yeah, you should read the book

3649
02:06:22.560 --> 02:06:24.880
and then go visit one of those sites.

3650
02:06:24.880 --> 02:06:25.713
Exactly, read the book.

3651
02:06:25.713 --> 02:06:27.970
Don't take, don't worry about me.

3652
02:06:27.970 --> 02:06:30.340
I'm the guy that the Self-Realization Fellowship

3653
02:06:30.340 --> 02:06:31.388
didn't even like.

3654
02:06:31.388 --> 02:06:34.570
(Rich) But you're an unlikely person to have

3655
02:06:34.570 --> 02:06:37.680
that kind of experience and then admit to it.

3656
02:06:37.680 --> 02:06:38.513
You know what I mean?

3657
02:06:38.513 --> 02:06:41.220
Like you have a practical, grounded perspective

3658
02:06:41.220 --> 02:06:42.053
over these things.
Yeah, well that happened.

3659
02:06:42.053 --> 02:06:44.400
So, that's very cool.

3660
02:06:44.400 --> 02:06:47.028
My Kerouac of choice is "The Dharma Bums."

3661
02:06:47.028 --> 02:06:50.393
I, "On the Road" was very important to me,

3662
02:06:51.310 --> 02:06:54.040
because it gives permission to be expansive.

3663
02:06:54.040 --> 02:06:59.040
It gives permission to reach for some expansive sense

3664
02:06:59.270 --> 02:07:04.040
of self and joy in the moment and not be someone who's

3665
02:07:04.040 --> 02:07:09.000
about collecting stuff and putting it in their stuff house.

3666
02:07:09.000 --> 02:07:10.660
And that's what you need to do.

3667
02:07:10.660 --> 02:07:14.467
Like I still am guided by that to some degree.

3668
02:07:14.467 --> 02:07:15.590
"The Dharma Bums" though,

3669
02:07:15.590 --> 02:07:17.490
it comes after "On the Road" has,

3670
02:07:17.490 --> 02:07:20.500
it is, "On the Road" is in the can.

3671
02:07:20.500 --> 02:07:21.930
Everyone loves it as publishers.

3672
02:07:21.930 --> 02:07:23.360
It's not out yet.

3673
02:07:23.360 --> 02:07:25.240
And he goes on one last road trip,

3674
02:07:25.240 --> 02:07:27.370
before it becomes this massive hit.

3675
02:07:27.370 --> 02:07:28.740
He's written, it it's all done,

3676
02:07:28.740 --> 02:07:30.760
